{"ID":"244","Name":"Improper Clearing of Heap Memory Before Release","Abstraction":"Variant","Structure":"Simple","Status":"Draft","Description":"The product uses realloc() to resize buffers that contain sensitive information.","WeaknessOrdinalities":[{"Ordinality":"Primary"}],"BackgroundDetails":["The realloc() function is commonly used to increase the size of a block of allocated memory. This operation often requires copying the contents of the old memory block into a new and larger block."],"CommonConsequences":[{"Scope":["Confidentiality","Other"],"Impact":["Read Memory","Other"],"Note":"\n\nSince realloc() leaves the contents of the original block intact but inaccessible to the program, this the program from being able to scrub sensitive data from memory. When sensitive data such as a password or an encryption key is not removed from memory, an attacker could use \"heap inspection\" to read the sensitive data using memory dumps or other methods.\n"}],"DemonstrativeExamples":[{"ID":"DX-148","Entries":[{"IntroText":"The following code calls realloc() on a buffer containing sensitive data:"},{"Nature":"Bad","Language":"C","ExampleCode":"```\n\tcleartext_buffer = get_secret();...\n\tcleartext_buffer = realloc(cleartext_buffer, 1024);\n\t...\n\tscrub_memory(cleartext_buffer, 1024);\n```"},{"BodyText":"There is an attempt to scrub the sensitive data from memory, but realloc() is used, so it could return a pointer to a different part of memory. The memory that was originally allocated for cleartext_buffer could still contain an uncleared copy of the data."}]}],"FunctionalAreas":["Memory Management"],"AffectedResources":["Memory"],"TaxonomyMappings":[{"TaxonomyName":"7 Pernicious Kingdoms","EntryName":"Heap Inspection"},{"TaxonomyName":"CERT C Secure Coding","EntryID":"MEM03-C","EntryName":"Clear sensitive information stored in reusable resources returned for reuse"},{"TaxonomyName":"Software Fault Patterns","EntryID":"SFP23","EntryName":"Exposed Data"}],"MappingNotes":{"Usage":"Allowed","Rationale":"This CWE entry is at the Variant level of abstraction, which is a preferred level of abstraction for mapping to the root causes of vulnerabilities.","Comments":"Carefully read both the name and description to ensure that this mapping is an appropriate fit. Do not try to 'force' a mapping to a lower-level Base/Variant simply to comply with this preferred level of abstraction.","Reasons":["Acceptable-Use"]},"References":[{"ExternalReferenceID":"REF-6","Authors":["Katrina Tsipenyuk","Brian Chess","Gary McGraw"],"Title":"Seven Pernicious Kingdoms: A Taxonomy of Software Security Errors","Publication":"NIST Workshop on Software Security Assurance Tools Techniques and Metrics","PublicationYear":"2005","PublicationMonth":"11","PublicationDay":"07","Publisher":"NIST","URL":"https://cwe.mitre.org/documents/sources/SevenPerniciousKingdoms.pdf"}],"ObservedExamples":[{"Reference":"CVE-2019-3733","Description":"Cryptography library does not clear heap memory before release","Link":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2019-3733"}],"RelatedWeaknesses":[{"Nature":"ChildOf","CweID":"226","ViewID":"1000","Ordinal":"Primary"},{"Nature":"CanPrecede","CweID":"669","ViewID":"1000"}],"ApplicablePlatforms":[{"Type":"Language","Class":"Memory-Unsafe","Prevalence":"Undetermined"},{"Type":"Language","Name":"C","Prevalence":"Undetermined"},{"Type":"Language","Name":"C++","Prevalence":"Undetermined"}],"AlternateTerms":[{"Term":"Heap Inspection","Roles":["Common-Name","Attack-Focused"]}],"ModesOfIntroduction":[{"Phase":["Implementation"]}],"DetectionMethods":[{"DetectionMethodID":"DM-14","Method":"Automated Static Analysis","Description":"Automated static analysis, commonly referred to as Static Application Security Testing (SAST), can find some instances of this weakness by analyzing source code (or binary/compiled code) without having to execute it. Typically, this is done by building a model of data flow and control flow, then searching for potentially-vulnerable patterns that connect \"sources\" (origins of input) with \"sinks\" (destinations where the data interacts with external components, a lower layer such as the OS, etc.)"}],"ContentHistory":[{"Type":"Submission","SubmissionNames":["7 Pernicious Kingdoms"],"SubmissionDate":"2006-07-19","SubmissionVersion":"Draft 3","SubmissionReleaseDate":"2006-07-19"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationOrganization":"KDM Analytics","ModificationDate":"2008-08-01","ModificationComment":"added/updated white box definitions","ModificationVersion":"1.0","ModificationReleaseDate":"2008-09-09"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2008-09-08","ModificationComment":"updated Applicable_Platforms, Name, Relationships, Other_Notes, Taxonomy_Mappings","ModificationVersion":"1.0","ModificationReleaseDate":"2008-09-09"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2008-10-14","ModificationComment":"updated Relationships","ModificationVersion":"1.0.1","ModificationReleaseDate":"2008-10-14"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2008-11-24","ModificationComment":"updated Relationships, Taxonomy_Mappings","ModificationVersion":"1.1","ModificationReleaseDate":"2008-11-25"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2009-05-27","ModificationComment":"updated Demonstrative_Examples, Name","ModificationVersion":"1.4","ModificationReleaseDate":"2009-05-27"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2009-10-29","ModificationComment":"updated Common_Consequences, Description, Other_Notes","ModificationVersion":"1.6","ModificationReleaseDate":"2009-10-29"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2010-12-13","ModificationComment":"updated Name","ModificationVersion":"1.11","ModificationReleaseDate":"2010-12-13"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2011-06-01","ModificationComment":"updated Common_Consequences","ModificationVersion":"1.13","ModificationReleaseDate":"2011-06-01"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2011-09-13","ModificationComment":"updated Relationships, Taxonomy_Mappings","ModificationVersion":"2.1","ModificationReleaseDate":"2011-09-13"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2012-05-11","ModificationComment":"updated Relationships","ModificationVersion":"2.2","ModificationReleaseDate":"2012-05-15"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2014-07-30","ModificationComment":"updated Relationships, Taxonomy_Mappings","ModificationVersion":"2.8","ModificationReleaseDate":"2014-07-31"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2017-11-08","ModificationComment":"updated Relationships, Taxonomy_Mappings, White_Box_Definitions","ModificationVersion":"3.0","ModificationReleaseDate":"2017-11-08"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2020-02-24","ModificationComment":"updated References, Relationships","ModificationVersion":"4.0","ModificationReleaseDate":"2020-02-24"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":"CWE Content Team","ModificationOrganization":"MITRE","ModificationDate":"2021-10-28","ModificationComment":"updated Demonstrative_Examples","ModificationVersion":"4.6","ModificationReleaseDate":"2021-10-28"},{"Type":"Modification","ModificationName":